CORE no-new-smt
main.c
--trace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
return_value_f\.length=
--
return_value\$\$f\.
^warning: ignoring
--
Assignments to the fields of a struct in a hidden function (one with a
__CPROVER_HIDE label) are hidden in traces, like the assignment to the
whole struct. They used to be shown, one step per field, for the
function's return value.
